    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d205">

                <pb facs="0197" n="191" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg191"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Sir
                            Julian Pauncefote.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-05-07"><hi rendition="#italic">May 7,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: The two Governments having provided
                    by legislation and regulations for the enforcement of the award of the Paris
                    Tribunal under the treaty of February 29, 1892, the time appears to have arrived
                    for carrying out the stipulation of article 7 of the convention.</p>
                <p>I am therefore directed by the President to invite the attention of Her Majesty’s
                    Government to the matter, to the end that with all convenient speed the two
                    Governments may cooperate in securing the adhesion to the award of other powers,
                    especially Russia and Japan.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
